rst comic to  start selling out arenas  and really put stand-up comedy on that  next level  from a business standpoint and what's  interesting  as we talk about uh this book breaking  down the fundamentals  of joke writing how to you know um  set up punch misdirect the audience  steve martin's approach to comedy was  actually  the absence of a punchline and he talks  about in his  book how he started to find comedy in  the  absence of structure in the absence of  a formula within comedy which i think  really  is what made him stand out from the  comedy at the time  was him looking at what's popular and  how can i do the opposite and make that  even more popular  and this book is not only just about his  process it's about  the early struggles of being a comedian  seriously  in san francisco performing in front of  a window to get people to come into the  empty venue he was performing at  so many amazing stories and this is  known in the comedy community as a must  read by the most well respected comics  in the game  this book gives you the most realistic  brutally honest transparent  just raw reality that is  the pursuit of stand-up comedy you know  um  even jerry seinfeld says on the cover  right here absolutely magnificent one of  the best books about comedy  and being a comedian ever written and  that's from jerry seinfeld  and this is coming from joel byers as  well which is me  and you probably forgot already  but it's all good steve martin's born  standing up a must read for anyone  that wants to pursue comedy as their  profession  and take it seriously must read and the  audiobook is really good because steve  actually reads it as well  check it out the next one  i killed when we're talking about  reality  okay and how steve martin's book gives  you that raw reality of  the early days of stand-up starting out  in stand-up and he traces his career to  the immense success  and his eventual um hiatus from stand up  and i say hiatus because i do feel like  he he 